  "notes": "Cash-basis city (receipts/disbursements statements) with accrual-style proprietary statements. Governmental beginning/ending balances are the printed beginning/ending fund balance of the governmental funds statement (p4), used as cash balance; identity 5,474,971 + 886,820 - 1,283,945 - 4,045,816 = 1,032,030. Governmental transfers out 4,045,816 equal business-type transfers in (water 4,140,329, sewer -91,892, sanitation -2,621; p6); matched. Business-type: user fees, grant income and interest from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Net Position (p6); operating expenses by line, total 636,120 (statement of activities p2 prints 636,121, rounding). Business-type roll-forward: 3,347,071 + 572,992 - 636,120 + 4,045,816 = 7,329,759. Balance sheet from government-wide Statement of Net Position total column (p1). Detail: the all-funds budgetary comparison schedule (p8) prints only fund totals (actual column; budget shown only for total receipts/disbursements, so line budget_final is null); recorded with fund = 'All funds' and the fund row name in department (so lines tie to the all-funds totals), transfers as signed other financing; the Debt service row is split into principal 25,000 and interest 4,152 from the Debt Service column on p4; its printed totals include the transfers. Its budgetary-basis figures differ from the statements (beginning balance 5,543,818, water disbursements include capital). Proprietary cash flow statement (p7) not recorded because basis is cash. Read pages 1-8 of 8",
  "decision_needed": [
